{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-trace/trace-reader-brief.md /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-trace/trace-packet-r2.json'","aggregated_output":"# The loss trace: was the fact extracted? (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief and the one\npacket you are given.\n\nEach point of your packet holds one **decisive item**: a statement an earlier reader, called reader B, cited for a frozen answer (its day,\ntitle, who said it, the passage and its meaning). Beside it is **every evidence item a system kept from that same article** (each with a\n`ref`, a summary and the passages it quotes); the list is empty when the system kept nothing from the article.\n\nFor each point, answer one question: does one of the kept items **state the decisive item's fact** — the same fact or figure, in any wording?\nName the kept item's `ref` that states it (the first if several do), or `none` when no kept item states it. Search the kept items for the\nfigure or the fact; do not name an item because it is related, from the same article, or about the same topic.\n\nReturn one JSON object per point, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"point\": 3, \"extracted\": \"<ref>\"|\"none\", \"why\": \"one sentence naming the figure or fact that decides it\"}`.\n[\n {\n  \"point\": 1,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n   \"title\": \"Can Micron Technology Become the New Nvidia?\",\n   \"who\": \"Micron (as reported by the author)\",\n   \"passage\": \"tight market conditions could last until 2028\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Micron (memory supplier)\",\n    \"what\": \"memory market stays tight: demand above supply, prices sharply higher, new industry capacity not online until 2027 or later\",\n    \"period\": \"until 2028\",\n    \"status\": \"forecast\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e#e177\",\n    \"summary\": \"The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and that their spending could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 2,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n   \"title\": \"Can Micron Technology Become the New Nvidia?\",\n   \"who\": \"the article's author\",\n   \"passage\": \"new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"the article's author\",\n    \"what\": \"new memory capacity comes online only in 2027 or later, so memory supply stays low\",\n    \"period\": \"at least the next year and a half\",\n    \"status\": \"view with a reason\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e#e177\",\n    \"summary\": \"The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and that their spending could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 3,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n   \"title\": \"Can Micron Technology Become the New Nvidia?\",\n   \"who\": \"Micron (guidance, as reported by the author)\",\n   \"passage\": \"Next quarter, it expects $50 billion in revenue\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Micron\",\n    \"what\": \"revenue guidance\",\n    \"how_much\": \"$50bn\",\n    \"period\": \"Micron's next fiscal quarter\",\n    \"status\": \"forecast (guidance)\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e#e177\",\n    \"summary\": \"The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and that their spending could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 4,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n   \"who\": \"Micron (guidance, as cited)\",\n   \"passage\": \"Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Micron guidance\",\n    \"what\": \"adjusted gross margin (memory pricing power)\",\n    \"how_much\": \"86%\",\n    \"period\": \"next quarter\",\n    \"status\": \"forecast\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e104\",\n    \"summary\": \"The author reports delays across NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems, without specifying a revised schedule.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e105\",\n    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, and data-center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e106\",\n    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said agentic AI is generating value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"“Agentic AI has arrived, doing productive work, generating real value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.”\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e107\",\n    \"summary\": \"The author says NVIDIA has $119 billion in supply commitments and that their significance depends on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"NVIDIA's $119B in supply commitments hinge on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools, which is a question the market appears to already be pricing in.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e108\",\n    \"summary\": \"Bloomberg Intelligence forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for custom ASICs through 2033, compared with 16% for AI accelerators.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Broadcom’s custom ASICs for Alphabet and Meta are eating the story, with Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e109\",\n    \"summary\": \"Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% higher year over year.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e110\",\n    \"summary\": \"Micron forecast an adjusted gross margin of 86% for next quarter.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter, above the peak gross margins NVIDIA ever achieved.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32#e111\",\n    \"summary\": \"Unspecified estimates put memory at half of total data-center spending in calendar 2027.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 5,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-08\",\n   \"title\": \"China to let AI firms buy Nvidia H200s, says report\",\n   \"who\": \"The Information, citing two unidentified people (via Bloomberg / Straits Times)\",\n   \"passage\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Chinese officials\",\n    \"what\": \"permission for top AI companies (Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek) to buy NVIDIA H200 chips, each on approval stating the number and reason\",\n    \"how_much\": \"a limited amount; total may be fewer than 200,000\",\n    \"condition\": \"approval per request; limited amount\",\n    \"status\": \"rumour\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c#e202\",\n    \"summary\": \"Nvidia is working to release its Rubin chip lineup in the second half of 2026.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia is now working to release an even more powerful line-up called Rubin in the second half of 2026 .\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 6,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n   \"who\": \"China's government (stated by Tom's Hardware)\",\n   \"passage\": \"Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy these AI processors\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Beijing\",\n    \"what\": \"Chinese companies not allowed to buy NVIDIA H200\",\n    \"status\": \"happened\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb#e415\",\n    \"summary\": \"Nvidia reportedly cut its authorized-client roster in Asia by more than half and tightened verification, including data-center inspections, contract checks, and end-user interviews, to reduce the risk of chips being diverted into China.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"According to the Financial Times , this roster cuts the number of authorized clients by more than half, with those remaining having passed tougher compliance inspections to ensure that they are genuine businesses, not shell companies designed to forward Nvidia GPUs and servers into China. Some of the steps that Nvidia took to help safeguard its chips reportedly included sending staff to customer data centers, contract verification, and interviewing end users.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 7,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n   \"who\": \"an unnamed tech executive (to the Financial Times)\",\n   \"passage\": \"all domestic suppliers are sold out and that they’re even considering less powerful chips\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"unnamed Chinese tech executive\",\n    \"what\": \"China's domestic AI-chip suppliers are sold out; buyers are considering less powerful chips\",\n    \"status\": \"claim\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb#e415\",\n    \"summary\": \"Nvidia reportedly cut its authorized-client roster in Asia by more than half and tightened verification, including data-center inspections, contract checks, and end-user interviews, to reduce the risk of chips being diverted into China.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"According to the Financial Times , this roster cuts the number of authorized clients by more than half, with those remaining having passed tougher compliance inspections to ensure that they are genuine businesses, not shell companies designed to forward Nvidia GPUs and servers into China. Some of the steps that Nvidia took to help safeguard its chips reportedly included sending staff to customer data centers, contract verification, and interviewing end users.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 8,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n   \"who\": \"US President (as reported)\",\n   \"passage\": \"President Donald Trump took a 180-degree turn in December 2025 and finally allowed Nvidia to export its H200 GPUs to select customers in the region\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"US President Trump\",\n    \"what\": \"allowed H200 exports to select customers in China\",\n    \"period\": \"December 2025\",\n    \"status\": \"happened\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb#e415\",\n    \"summary\": \"Nvidia reportedly cut its authorized-client roster in Asia by more than half and tightened verification, including data-center inspections, contract checks, and end-user interviews, to reduce the risk of chips being diverted into China.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"According to the Financial Times , this roster cuts the number of authorized clients by more than half, with those remaining having passed tougher compliance inspections to ensure that they are genuine businesses, not shell companies designed to forward Nvidia GPUs and servers into China. Some of the steps that Nvidia took to help safeguard its chips reportedly included sending staff to customer data centers, contract verification, and interviewing end users.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 9,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n   \"who\": \"Sharon AI (counterparty disclosure, reported by SemiAnalysis)\",\n   \"passage\": \"Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Sharon AI disclosed\",\n    \"what\": \"total value of NVIDIA's backstop on Sharon's 72MW Australian AI factory (up to 40,000 GB300)\",\n    \"how_much\": \"$4.88B; implied floor ~$2.33/hr/GPU\",\n    \"period\": \"six years\",\n    \"condition\": \"up to 40,000 GB300s\",\n    \"status\": \"happened\",\n    \"status_note\": \"announced June 2026\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates Nvidia’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue estimates are materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts AI debt financing will exceed $7 trillion outstanding by 2029, driven by AI IT and data-center capital needs.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"AI Debt Financing will become a multi-trillion-dollar credit market, with over $7T of debt outstanding by 2029 driven both by AI IT Capex and AI Datacenter Capex needs for Neoclouds, datacenter builders, and even hyperscalers.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital expenditure, including AI IT equipment and the data centers that house it, will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts cumulative AI capital expenditure from 2024 through 2029 will reach about $11.1 trillion and says credit markets will be its main funding source.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay backstops that guarantee minimum revenue on GPU capacity.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started backstopping data-center leases as part of its Neocloud support.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop programme typically lasts six years and commits Nvidia to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI announced a six-year Nvidia backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs at its 72MW Australian AI factory, disclosing a total backstop value of $4.88 billion and an implied average floor of about $2.33 per GPU-hour.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI guides that by mid-2027 its footprint will reach 132MW, including 102MW contracted, and its total Nvidia GPU count will exceed 55,000, including the 40,000 backstopped GB300s.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e80\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 360MW Batam, Indonesia AI cluster with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; SemiAnalysis says it will likely be housed in a DayOne facility at Kabil Industrial Tech Park.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e81\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus expects customer revenue of $25 billion to $30 billion over six years for its Batam project.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e82\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says many Neoclouds are in advanced negotiations with Nvidia over backstops, while others are considering the programme.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia, and there are still others that are considering engaging with the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 10,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n   \"who\": \"Firmus (announced June 29, 2026; reported by SemiAnalysis)\",\n   \"passage\": \"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop.\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Firmus\",\n    \"what\": \"a second announced NVIDIA-backstopped cluster\",\n    \"how_much\": \"360MW\",\n    \"period\": \"announced June 29, 2026\",\n    \"status\": \"happened\",\n    \"status_note\": \"announced\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates Nvidia’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue estimates are materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts AI debt financing will exceed $7 trillion outstanding by 2029, driven by AI IT and data-center capital needs.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"AI Debt Financing will become a multi-trillion-dollar credit market, with over $7T of debt outstanding by 2029 driven both by AI IT Capex and AI Datacenter Capex needs for Neoclouds, datacenter builders, and even hyperscalers.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital expenditure, including AI IT equipment and the data centers that house it, will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts cumulative AI capital expenditure from 2024 through 2029 will reach about $11.1 trillion and says credit markets will be its main funding source.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay backstops that guarantee minimum revenue on GPU capacity.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started backstopping data-center leases as part of its Neocloud support.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop programme typically lasts six years and commits Nvidia to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI announced a six-year Nvidia backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs at its 72MW Australian AI factory, disclosing a total backstop value of $4.88 billion and an implied average floor of about $2.33 per GPU-hour.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI guides that by mid-2027 its footprint will reach 132MW, including 102MW contracted, and its total Nvidia GPU count will exceed 55,000, including the 40,000 backstopped GB300s.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e80\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 360MW Batam, Indonesia AI cluster with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; SemiAnalysis says it will likely be housed in a DayOne facility at Kabil Industrial Tech Park.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e81\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus expects customer revenue of $25 billion to $30 billion over six years for its Batam project.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e82\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says many Neoclouds are in advanced negotiations with Nvidia over backstops, while others are considering the programme.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia, and there are still others that are considering engaging with the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 11,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n   \"who\": \"Firmus\",\n   \"passage\": \"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"Firmus\",\n    \"what\": \"expected customer revenue on the backstopped Batam cluster (part above the backstop is shared with NVIDIA)\",\n    \"how_much\": \"$25B-$30B\",\n    \"period\": \"over six years\",\n    \"status\": \"forecast\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates Nvidia’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue estimates are materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts AI debt financing will exceed $7 trillion outstanding by 2029, driven by AI IT and data-center capital needs.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"AI Debt Financing will become a multi-trillion-dollar credit market, with over $7T of debt outstanding by 2029 driven both by AI IT Capex and AI Datacenter Capex needs for Neoclouds, datacenter builders, and even hyperscalers.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital expenditure, including AI IT equipment and the data centers that house it, will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts cumulative AI capital expenditure from 2024 through 2029 will reach about $11.1 trillion and says credit markets will be its main funding source.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay backstops that guarantee minimum revenue on GPU capacity.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started backstopping data-center leases as part of its Neocloud support.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop programme typically lasts six years and commits Nvidia to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI announced a six-year Nvidia backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs at its 72MW Australian AI factory, disclosing a total backstop value of $4.88 billion and an implied average floor of about $2.33 per GPU-hour.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI guides that by mid-2027 its footprint will reach 132MW, including 102MW contracted, and its total Nvidia GPU count will exceed 55,000, including the 40,000 backstopped GB300s.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e80\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 360MW Batam, Indonesia AI cluster with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; SemiAnalysis says it will likely be housed in a DayOne facility at Kabil Industrial Tech Park.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e81\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus expects customer revenue of $25 billion to $30 billion over six years for its Batam project.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e82\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says many Neoclouds are in advanced negotiations with Nvidia over backstops, while others are considering the programme.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia, and there are still others that are considering engaging with the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 12,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n   \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n   \"passage\": \"Nvidia’s backstop program is only getting started, and we see announcements coming faster every quarter. Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n    \"what\": \"more NVIDIA backstops exist but are not public; many neoclouds in negotiation; announcements accelerating\",\n    \"status\": \"claim\",\n    \"status_note\": \"existing undisclosed backstops; more deals are a forecast\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates Nvidia’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue estimates are materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts AI debt financing will exceed $7 trillion outstanding by 2029, driven by AI IT and data-center capital needs.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"AI Debt Financing will become a multi-trillion-dollar credit market, with over $7T of debt outstanding by 2029 driven both by AI IT Capex and AI Datacenter Capex needs for Neoclouds, datacenter builders, and even hyperscalers.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital expenditure, including AI IT equipment and the data centers that house it, will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts cumulative AI capital expenditure from 2024 through 2029 will reach about $11.1 trillion and says credit markets will be its main funding source.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay backstops that guarantee minimum revenue on GPU capacity.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started backstopping data-center leases as part of its Neocloud support.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop programme typically lasts six years and commits Nvidia to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI announced a six-year Nvidia backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs at its 72MW Australian AI factory, disclosing a total backstop value of $4.88 billion and an implied average floor of about $2.33 per GPU-hour.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI guides that by mid-2027 its footprint will reach 132MW, including 102MW contracted, and its total Nvidia GPU count will exceed 55,000, including the 40,000 backstopped GB300s.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e80\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 360MW Batam, Indonesia AI cluster with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; SemiAnalysis says it will likely be housed in a DayOne facility at Kabil Industrial Tech Park.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e81\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus expects customer revenue of $25 billion to $30 billion over six years for its Batam project.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e82\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says many Neoclouds are in advanced negotiations with Nvidia over backstops, while others are considering the programme.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia, and there are still others that are considering engaging with the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 13,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n   \"who\": \"The Information (prior reporting)\",\n   \"passage\": \"NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"NVIDIA (per The Information)\",\n    \"what\": \"negotiating to guarantee OpenAI's lease of a large Ohio data center\",\n    \"how_much\": \"the data center could cost as much as $500 billion if fully built (asset cost, not the guarantee amount)\",\n    \"condition\": \"in negotiation; nothing signed\",\n    \"status\": \"rumour\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e3\",\n    \"summary\": \"The Information reported on July 1 that NVIDIA was providing financial guarantees to young GPU cloud providers and would repurchase unsold capacity at a pre-agreed price if they failed to find enough renters.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"On July 1, according to the technology news outlet The Information, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs—if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e4\",\n    \"summary\": \"Under the reported arrangements, NVIDIA will receive a share of participating cloud providers’ revenue, with the rate declining over each contract term.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"In return, NVIDIA will receive a percentage of these cloud providers’ revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the term of the contract.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e5\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus and Sharon AI have joined NVIDIA’s reported cloud-provider program, according to the report, which said three executives with existing NVIDIA business ties confirmed the arrangement.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e6\",\n    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced on July 1 a business model combining revenue sharing and credit support to help AI cloud providers procure its infrastructure without paying the full capital expenditure upfront.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"On July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e7\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs; Firmus is constructing a Batam DSX AI Factory campus planned for up to 360 MW and 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, while Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e8\",\n    \"summary\": \"The Information had reported that NVIDIA was negotiating financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of an Ohio data center, whose full build-out could cost as much as $500 billion.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e9\",\n    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA’s May 2026 regulatory filing, covering the quarter ended in April, disclosed that it had added $3.5 billion in guarantees for customer data-center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"According to a regulatory filing submitted by NVIDIA in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 14,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n   \"who\": \"NVIDIA (May 2026 quarterly filing)\",\n   \"passage\": \"NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n    \"what\": \"guarantees of customer data center leases, in exchange for rights to buy their shares\",\n    \"how_much\": \"an additional $3.5 billion\",\n    \"period\": \"quarter ended April 2026 (filed May)\",\n    \"status\": \"happened\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e3\",\n    \"summary\": \"The Information reported on July 1 that NVIDIA was providing financial guarantees to young GPU cloud providers and would repurchase unsold capacity at a pre-agreed price if they failed to find enough renters.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"On July 1, according to the technology news outlet The Information, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs—if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e4\",\n    \"summary\": \"Under the reported arrangements, NVIDIA will receive a share of participating cloud providers’ revenue, with the rate declining over each contract term.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"In return, NVIDIA will receive a percentage of these cloud providers’ revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the term of the contract.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e5\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus and Sharon AI have joined NVIDIA’s reported cloud-provider program, according to the report, which said three executives with existing NVIDIA business ties confirmed the arrangement.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e6\",\n    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA announced on July 1 a business model combining revenue sharing and credit support to help AI cloud providers procure its infrastructure without paying the full capital expenditure upfront.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"On July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e7\",\n    \"summary\": \"Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs; Firmus is constructing a Batam DSX AI Factory campus planned for up to 360 MW and 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, while Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e8\",\n    \"summary\": \"The Information had reported that NVIDIA was negotiating financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of an Ohio data center, whose full build-out could cost as much as $500 billion.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45#e9\",\n    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA’s May 2026 regulatory filing, covering the quarter ended in April, disclosed that it had added $3.5 billion in guarantees for customer data-center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"According to a regulatory filing submitted by NVIDIA in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"point\": 15,\n  \"decisive_item\": {\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n   \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n   \"passage\": \"Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n    \"what\": \"NVIDIA backstops datacenter leases for neoclouds (a second kind of obligation)\",\n    \"status\": \"happened\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"kept_from_that_article\": [\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e71\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says its supply-chain tracking indicates Nvidia’s second-half 2026 shipment-volume and revenue estimates are materially higher than the general market’s estimates.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e72\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts AI debt financing will exceed $7 trillion outstanding by 2029, driven by AI IT and data-center capital needs.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"AI Debt Financing will become a multi-trillion-dollar credit market, with over $7T of debt outstanding by 2029 driven both by AI IT Capex and AI Datacenter Capex needs for Neoclouds, datacenter builders, and even hyperscalers.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e73\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts annual AI capital expenditure, including AI IT equipment and the data centers that house it, will exceed $2 trillion in calendar 2028.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Annual AI Capex – including GPUs, networking, storage and attached CPU compute as well as for the Datacenters to house AI compute – will be well north of $2T in 2028.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e74\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis forecasts cumulative AI capital expenditure from 2024 through 2029 will reach about $11.1 trillion and says credit markets will be its main funding source.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Cumulative AI Capex from 2024 to 2029 will reach ~$11.1T, and credit markets will be the main funding source for this buildout.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e75\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started providing Neoclouds take-or-pay backstops that guarantee minimum revenue on GPU capacity.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"This is why Nvidia has stepped in and has started backstopping GPU rental offtakes themselves . In the backstop program, Nvidia provides a take-or-pay commitment to Neoclouds – a minimum revenue guarantee on the underlying GPU capacity.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e76\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Nvidia has started backstopping data-center leases as part of its Neocloud support.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Here, Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e77\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says Nvidia’s backstop programme typically lasts six years and commits Nvidia to purchase compute at pre-agreed prices that vary over the term.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e78\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI announced a six-year Nvidia backstop for up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs at its 72MW Australian AI factory, disclosing a total backstop value of $4.88 billion and an implied average floor of about $2.33 per GPU-hour.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e79\",\n    \"summary\": \"SharonAI guides that by mid-2027 its footprint will reach 132MW, including 102MW contracted, and its total Nvidia GPU count will exceed 55,000, including the 40,000 backstopped GB300s.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e80\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus announced a 360MW Batam, Indonesia AI cluster with an Nvidia backstop on June 29, 2026; SemiAnalysis says it will likely be housed in a DayOne facility at Kabil Industrial Tech Park.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e81\",\n    \"summary\": \"Firmus expects customer revenue of $25 billion to $30 billion over six years for its Batam project.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"ref\": \"gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6#e82\",\n    \"summary\": \"SemiAnalysis says many Neoclouds are in advanced negotiations with Nvidia over backstops, while others are considering the programme.\",\n    \"passages\": [\n     \"Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia, and there are still others that are considering engaging with the backstop program.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-trace/trace-packet-r2.json\\\")); print(json.dumps([x for x in p if x[\\\"point\\\"] in (10,11,12)], ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
